<title>UK: Severn Trent aims for further reorganisation.</title>
<headline>Severn Trent aims for further reorganisation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>British water and sewerage company Severn Trent Plc said on Tuesday it had taken a 20 million stg provision in its full-year accounts as part of cover for a 29 million stg reorganisation.</p>
<p>It said the reorganisation of operational activities at its water and sewerage business should start to see cost savings in 1997/98 which would reach 12 million stg a year by 2000/01.</p>
<p>The company said the focus of the reorganisation would be on &quot;delivering specific customer service and asset management productivity.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44171 542 7717</p>
